        "id": 223786,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-24T11:52:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1. No. The Ocean is only a land for particular purposes (Powers and Blight). Growth is not on that list, so Finder cannot place Presence in the Ocean during Growth. There are plenty of other ways to get Presence in the Ocean, however.</p>\n<p>1a. Yes, moving an Invader&nbsp;to the Ocean does trigger its drowning.</p>\n<p>2. On your examples (including the one in text): Yes, moving an Invader to the Ocean to Drown it does trigger Responsibilities of the Dead. On the others:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>No, does not trigger.</li>\n\t<li>No, does not trigger.</li>\n\t<li>No, does not trigger.</li>\n\t<li>Irrelevant, since none of those would trigger.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Basically it's only Finder's \"fault\" if it happens immediately.</p>\n<p>(Terminology is still a bit in flux, but one concept that's being formalized in this expansion is the notion of one action \"triggering\" off of another, the way Vengeance of the Dead or Drowning triggers off of certain other effects.)</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
